.TH CHTTP_BASIC_AUTH 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_basic_auth \- build an HTTP Basic auth header value (default allocator)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

char *chttp_basic_auth(const char *username, const char *password);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a static inline wrapper around chttp_basic_auth_mp() that
gives NULL for the memory management procedures, so the function uses
malloc and free.

RFC 7617 SS2 makes the colon the one delimiter of the encoded
"user-id:password" string, and a recipient cuts that string at its
FIRST colon.  A username with a colon in it is therefore not
transmittable without ambiguity, and the function rejects it.  Without
that rejection, the username "a:b" with the password "c" encodes to
the same bytes as the username "a" with the password "b:c", so a
caller that asks for one identity sends a different one.  A colon in
the password needs no escape, and the function builds the string as
the caller asks.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
username  The username. It must not be NULL and must not contain a
          colon (':'), but it can be empty.
password  The password. It must not be NULL, but it can be empty and
          can contain colons.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new "Basic <base64>" string on success.
NULL if the allocation fails, if username or password is NULL, or if
username contains a colon.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_basic_auth_mp (3),
.BR chttp_base64_encode (3)
